{"id": "EUVD-2026-96617", "enisaUuid": "659b91e8-aee7-3954-a71f-9b9aed9d06cf", "description": "JeecgBoot through 3.9.5 contains a missing authorization vulnerability in the queryUserRoles handler of SystemApiController that lets authenticated users read any user's role codes. Low-privileged attackers can send GET requests to /sys/api/queryUserRoles with an arbitrary username to enumerate role assignments and identify administrator accounts.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T21:49:57", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T02:39:58", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/AnkesKasty/cve-request-poc/blob/a7b6d1423555812d8efa26c91c5d0683164b31e5/JeecgBoot/poc_sys_api_credential_family.py", "https://github.com/jeecgboot/JeecgBoot/blob/e3b9dc0aefe1943d9772b026f64ed671a7c82802/jeecg-boot/jeecg-module-system/jeecg-system-biz/src/main/java/org/jeecg/modules/api/controller/SystemApiController.java#L472-L475", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/jeecgboot-through-3.9.5-missing-authorization-via-sys-api-queryuserroles"], "aliases": ["GHSA-crh3-f6w4-mf88", "CVE-2026-108678"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "a55220e4-5058-380b-af90-e785d1ed9e0b", "product": {"name": "JeecgBoot", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.9.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ed93aaf6-30cd-3141-8dad-77d1171408bb", "vendor": {"name": "jeecgboot"}}], "isExploited": false}